{
  "subject": "Basic Mathematics",
  "topic": "Exponents and Logarithms",
  "introduction": "Exponents and logarithms are inverses of each other. Logarithms convert multiplication into addition and powers into products, making complex expressions solvable. The change of base formula and log properties are essential SIMAK tools.",
  "key_formulas": [
    {
      "name": "Log definition",
      "formula": "\\log_a b = c \\Leftrightarrow a^c = b"
    },
    {
      "name": "Product rule",
      "formula": "\\log_a(xy) = \\log_a x + \\log_a y"
    },
    {
      "name": "Quotient rule",
      "formula": "\\log_a(x/y) = \\log_a x - \\log_a y"
    },
    {
      "name": "Power rule",
      "formula": "\\log_a(x^n) = n\\log_a x"
    },
    {
      "name": "Change of base",
      "formula": "\\log_a b = \\frac{\\log b}{\\log a} = \\frac{\\ln b}{\\ln a}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Log of 1",
      "formula": "\\log_a 1 = 0"
    },
    {
      "name": "Log of base",
      "formula": "\\log_a a = 1"
    },
    {
      "name": "Reciprocal",
      "formula": "\\log_a b = \\frac{1}{\\log_b a}"
    }
  ],
  "tips_and_tricks": [
    "log₁₀ is written as log; logₑ is written as ln.",
    "To solve log equations: make both sides log of same base, then equate arguments.",
    "For exponential equations: take log of both sides.",
    "Remember: a^(log_a x) = x (inverse property).",
    "log(a×b) = log a + log b — multiplication becomes addition!",
    "When solving log₂(x) = 3: x = 2³ = 8."
  ],
  "worked_examples": [
    {
      "title": "Example 1: System of exponential equations",
      "question": "Solve: 6/3^x - 6/2^x = 1 and 3^x - 2^x = 1. Find 6^x.",
      "solution": [
        "Step 1: Let a = 3^x, b = 2^x.",
        "Step 2: Equations become: 6/b - 6/a = 1 → 6(a-b)/(ab) = 1.",
        "Step 3: From 2nd equation: a - b = 1.",
        "Step 4: Substitute: 6(1)/(ab) = 1 → ab = 6.",
        "Step 5: 6^x = 3^x × 2^x = a × b = 6."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Example 2: Nested logarithm simplification",
      "question": "Simplify log₂(log₃(log₄ 4)).",
      "solution": [
        "Step 1: log₄(4) = 1 (log of base = 1).",
        "Step 2: log₃(1) = 0 (log of 1 = 0).",
        "Step 3: log₂(0) is undefined! So the expression has no real value.",
        "Alternative: log₂(log₃(log₄ 64)):",
        "log₄(64) = log₄(4³) = 3. log₃(3) = 1. log₂(1) = 0."
      ]
    }
  ],
